@page
@model PrivacyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Manifest";
}

<div class="container mt-5">
    <div class="bg-lyra-dark text-light p-5 rounded shadow-sm">
        <h1 class="mb-4 fw-bold">
            <i class="bi bi-eye-slash-fill me-2"></i> Privacy Manifest
        </h1>

        <p class="text-light-emphasis fs-5 mb-4">
            In LYRA, privacy isn't just a checkbox. It's a boundary. A handshake. A pact between systems.
        </p>

        <hr class="border-secondary" />

        <h5 class="fw-semibold mt-4">
            <i class="bi bi-shield-shaded me-2 text-light"></i> What LYRA Sees
        </h5>
        <ul class="text-light-emphasis">
            <li>Hashed passwords only — no readable secrets, ever</li>
            <li>Service-level metadata: when, who, and how — not what</li>
            <li>Access relationships between trusted systems</li>
            <li>Validations of integrity, not inspections of content</li>
            <li>All audit logs are stored securely and access-controlled</li>
        </ul>

        <h5 class="fw-semibold mt-4">
            <i class="bi bi-eye me-2 text-light"></i> What LYRA Refuses to See
        </h5>
        <ul class="text-light-emphasis">
            <li>No personal user data or session payloads</li>
            <li>No cookies beyond security essentials</li>
            <li>No tracking, profiling, or fingerprinting</li>
            <li>No metrics unless explicitly enabled</li>
            <li>No plaintext secrets or keys stored</li>
        </ul>

        <h5 class="fw-semibold mt-4">
            <i class="bi bi-link-45deg me-2 text-light"></i> Trust is Contextual
        </h5>
        <p class="text-light-emphasis">
            LYRA defines trust between systems using precise, transparent policies. Nothing is assumed. Every permission is granted deliberately.
        </p>

        <h5 class="fw-semibold mt-4">
            <i class="bi bi-box-arrow-in-right me-2 text-light"></i> Self-Hosted. Yours Alone.
        </h5>
        <p class="text-light-emphasis">
            LYRA.Server runs in <span class="fw-bold text-light">your environment</span>, with <span class="fw-bold text-light">your rules</span>. No external APIs. No backdoors. You own the keys.
        </p>

        <h5 class="fw-semibold mt-4">
            <i class="bi bi-person-lines-fill me-2"></i> Maintained By
        </h5>
        <p class="text-light-emphasis">
            Built and maintained by <strong>Yurii Pasternak</strong> (<a href="mailto:pasternak2048@gmail.com" class="text-info">pasternak2048@gmail.com</a>).<br />
            View the project on <a href="https://github.com/pasternak2048" class="text-info" target="_blank">GitHub</a>.
        </p>

        <hr class="border-secondary" />

        <h5 class="fw-semibold mt-4">
            <i class="bi bi-shield-check me-2 text-light"></i> Your Privacy, Our Priority
        </h5>
        <p class="text-light-emphasis">
            LYRA is built with privacy by design and default. We encourage responsible data handling and are committed to ensuring your systems communicate securely without compromising user trust.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>